      "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=2,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[5-2X].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-2$ and $b=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[5-2X] & =(-2)^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
